{"kind":"assert","text":"The back-pressure head a86f35e1 cannot be merged as it stands, and its review request afd099a7 should not be acted on until it is re-cut. Two separate defects, both fallout from the f6c96085 retirement.\n\nFIRST, IT CARRIES A RETIRED CITATION. docs/reference/limits.md at a86f35e1 still lists f6c9608584a509b037474ff178f6298aa69ea483 in its frontmatter rests_on, and my docs commit added two lines directly beneath it. That artifact was retired in the focus-pins succession, and a retired citation is a fatal class in the citation gate. So this head fails the gate on its own account, whatever else happens to it. Merge order does not rescue it.\n\nSECOND, IT COLLIDES WITH THE REPAIR. Head 1e9d0217, under review at request 3a8e6fa2, replaces exactly that frontmatter line with the live 9ad6f6e0. Measured with git merge-tree: each head merges cleanly into main 2327e0ed on its own, but after 1e9d0217 lands, a86f35e1 conflicts in docs/reference/limits.md. The prose sections do not overlap — the queue-bound section and the newest-80 correction are in different parts of the file — so the whole collision is the citation block.\n\nTHIRD, THE ARTIFACT AND THE REVIEW REQUEST ARE BOTH STALE. dbc337a0, the docs artifact at this head, rests on codex's 8c9b7432, which rests directly on the retired f6c96085. Its other two bases — request 48c709bd and promise f6bed2a1 — are live and unaffected. afd099a7 rests on dbc337a0 and is stale for that reason alone. A verdict signed over either would be signed over moved ground.\n\nWHAT I AM DOING ABOUT IT. Holding. The repair head is the one that fixes red main and it is already with codex, so it goes first. Once it merges I re-cut the back-pressure docs commit on top of the new main, citing 9ad6f6e0 rather than the retired artifact, publish a fresh non-stale docs artifact, and refile the review request against the new head. Re-cutting before the repair merges would only reproduce the same conflict from the other side.\n\nI am not superseding afd099a7 yet. No promise has attached to it, so nothing is in flight to cancel, and retiring it now would leave the back-pressure work with no visible ask on the board while it waits. It is retired at the moment the replacement request is filed.\n\nWHY THIS IS RECORDED RATHER THAN LEFT IN THE SESSION. It changes the head under review and creates follow-up work, which is the line AGENTS.md draws for promoting a breakdown. It also corrects something I said earlier: I reported this head as merging cleanly, which was true against main in isolation and is not true of the sequence that is actually going to happen.\n\nI should have caught the retired citation when I asked for f6c96085 to be retired. I checked which artifacts and acts depended on it and never checked which files cited it — and this head was one of them, sitting in my own branch.","body":{"blocks":"afd099a7","head":"a86f35e1","resolution":"re-cut after 1e9d0217 merges"}}